INSERT INTO `mod_lore_codex_entry` (`ID`, `Kind`, `Zone`, `SortOrder`, `Faction`, `RequiredState`, `Title`, `Body`, `Sources`) VALUES
(352400, 0, 3524, 0, 0, 0, 'Azuremyst Isle', 'Azuremyst Isle is the southern of the two isles that lie off the northern coast of Kalimdor, a misty country of blue-needled pines, purple blossoms and quiet beaches. In ancient days the night elf empire left it unsettled on purpose, a wild hunting ground, and the ruins of their works still crumble at Wrathscale Point. For centuries its chief inhabitants were the furbolgs of the Stillpine and Bristlelimb tribes. Then the sky caught fire. The Exodar, the dimensional ship the draenei had seized from Tempest Keep, streaked over northern Kalimdor shedding crystals and came down crippled on the western side of the isle. The survivors have made the largest piece of its hull their new home. The crash scattered irradiated crystals across the land, poisoning a lake and maddening beasts and wildkin alike. From the outpost of Azure Watch the draenei work to heal the damage, even as naga, Venture Company goblins and blood elves prowl the island.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Azuremyst_Isle (geography, kaldorei hunting ground, ruins, two furbolg tribes, crash, crystal storm); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Exodar (Velen''s raid on Tempest Keep, infiltrated blood elves sabotaged the vessel, shed crystals over northern Kalimdor, crashed on the western side of Azuremyst); quests 9294, 9455, 9456, 9566 (crystal contamination); page_text 2919-2920 (Kael''thas letter); quests 9506, 9513'),
(352401, 1, 3524, 1, 0, 0, 'Ammen Vale', 'Ammen Vale is a small, hill-sheltered island on the eastern side of Azuremyst, cut off from the rest of the isle by the Crystalbrook River. When the Exodar broke apart, one section of the ship plunged into this valley, and those who woke from long suspension among its wreckage found smoking debris, scattered escape pods and the red glow of irradiated crystals all around them. Many had died. Beside the vale''s graveyard a grieving draenei stands over the marker of his beloved Luhanaa, wishing it had been him and swearing vengeance on whoever brought the ship down. A path leads west across the river to Azure Watch, the survivors'' road to the rest of their people.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Ammen_Vale (small island separated by the Crystalbrook, pods, crystals, wreckage); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Azuremyst_Isle (eastern side is Ammen Vale, sheltered by hills); quest 9279 description and reward text (suspension for weeks, only those in this part of the ship remain); quest 9283 (red glow of irradiated power crystals); creature_text 17073 Draenei Mourner; quest 9313 (path west across the Crystalbrook to Azure Watch)'),
(352402, 1, 3524, 2, 0, 0, 'Crash Site', 'The Crash Site is the broken section of the Exodar that came to rest in Ammen Vale, and it has become the refuge of everyone who lived through the fall. Inside its central chamber the priest Zalduun tends the wounded, while Proenitus rallies those who can still help and Vindicator Aldar sees to the camp''s defense. The healing crystals are nearly drained, and the only substitute at hand is the blood of the vale moths, a choice the draenei make with regret, for needless killing is not their way. Technician Zhanaa labors over a damaged holographic emitter, short of spare parts, in the hope of finding other survivors beyond the vale.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Ammen_Vale (Crash Site became the refuge for survivors); quest 9409 (Zalduun tending the wounded inside the central chamber); quests 9280, 9369 description and reward text (moth blood, indiscriminate killing is not the draenei way); quests 9305, 9312, 9313, 9314 (emitter, contact with Dyvuun at Azure Watch); quest 9311 reward text (Aldar will deal with the remaining blood elves)'),
(352403, 1, 3524, 3, 0, 0, 'Silverline Lake', 'South of the Crash Site, Silverline Lake took one of the Exodar''s power crystals straight into its waters. The irradiated crystal poisoned the lake, and the plants and animals that drank from it began to change. Mutated root lashers now choke the Ammen Fields to the west, the breeding ground of the vale''s lashers, where flowers bloom an unnatural red, and strange volatile creatures have sprung up near the fallen power cores. Botanist Taerix has a theory on how the lake might be healed, if only she can study samples taken from the mutated lashers.', 'quest 9293 description (lake contaminated by a power crystal, mutated lashers in the Ammen Fields to the west); quest 9294 description and reward text (lake to the south, neutralizing agent, unsure how long it will last, crystal should be removed); quest 9799 (Ammen Fields primary breeding ground of lashers, corrupted red flowers); quest 10302 (volatile mutations near the irradiated power cores); DB spawns: Irradiated Power Crystal 181433 in area 3528, Mutated Root Lasher and Corrupted Flower in 3560'),
(352404, 1, 3524, 4, 0, 0, 'Nestlewood', 'The wooded thickets and hills of Nestlewood, south of the Crash Site, are home to the Nestlewood owlkin. Many were twisted by the contamination from the crash and turned violent, while others remain untouched. Rather than wipe out the flock, the draenei carry an inoculating crystal prepared by Botanist Taerix to shield the healthy birds, and put down only those already too far gone. The owlkin had also carried off devices salvaged from the ship, and Technician Zhanaa needed those parts to repair her emitter. The inoculated birds take the crystal in very different ways: some seem overjoyed, some confused, and some plainly did not like what just happened.', 'quest 9303 description and reward text (inoculum for unaffected owlkin, the others must be killed, not wiping out the owlkin population); quest 9305 (owlkin carried off salvage, Nestlewood Thicket and Hills to the south); creature_text 16518 Nestlewood Owlkin emotes; DB spawns: Mutated Owlkin and Nestlewood Owlkin, Emitter Spare Part in 3529/3559'),
(352405, 1, 3524, 5, 0, 0, 'Shadow Ridge', 'Shadow Ridge rises beyond Silverline Lake on the southwestern edge of Ammen Vale. The survivors believed their scouting of the vale complete, yet reports of unusual activity on the ridge keep reaching the Crash Site, and one scout, Tolaan, has not come back. Blood elves have made camp along it. Their scouts patrol the slopes, vowing that no survivor will leave the valley alive, and a surveyor named Candress keeps to their camp.', 'quest 9309 description (unusual activity on Shadow Ridge, southwest across Silverline Lake, scouting thought thorough); quest 9309 reward text (Tolaan ambushed by blood elves); creature_text 16521 Blood Elf Scout; page_text 2906 (Blood Elf Plans, signed S.); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Ammen_Vale (Sunfury settled Shadow Ridge, Candress their leader); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Ammen_Vale (Sunfury outpost on Shadow Ridge, TBC tag)'),
(352406, 1, 3524, 6, 0, 0, 'The Sacred Grove', 'Nestled in the hills of northwestern Ammen Vale, the Sacred Grove is the home of the Spirit of the Vale. The violent arrival of the draenei threw the elements here out of balance: the enraged spirits of earth turned on the spirits of air, fire and water that came to calm them, and the grove is still a battlefield. The spirit has little love for the newcomers, yet it receives the draenei shaman who seek it, teaching that earth is the foundation on which all other elements rest. Shamanism is only now being relearned among the draenei, and many of their people distrust it, so a balance struck here is a hopeful sign.', 'quest 9449 description and reward text (grove in the hills to the northwest, imbalance, earth as foundation, bold to seek my wisdom after what your people have done); quest 9450 (earth spirits turned on the other elements); quest 9451 reward text (balance between the earth of this world and the draenei, those who do not approve of our ways); quest 9421 reward text (shamanism only now being relearned, not popular); DB spawns: Restless Spirit of Earth, Spirits of Air, Water and Fire, Spirit of the Vale 17087 in 3561'),
(352407, 1, 3524, 7, 0, 0, 'Azure Watch', 'Azure Watch is the outpost the Hand of Argus raised in the forest west of the Crystalbrook, within sight of the wrecked Exodar. Exarch Menelaous commands it, and its artificers, healers and trainers serve the many injured draenei who pass through. Technician Dyvuun works an emitter here in the hope of reaching survivors elsewhere on the isle, and a mysterious guest, a night elf found unconscious by the river, lies here in the care of its healers. A furbolg, Arugoo of the Stillpine, waits in the village beside a carved totem, whose symbols the cryptographer Aurren believes hold the key to speaking with the Stillpine tribe.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Azure_Watch (Hand of Argus forward outpost, artificers built it); npc_text of Exarch Menelaous (gaze upon the Exodar); quest 9463 (so many injured draenei passing through Azure Watch, guest found by the Crystalbrook); quests 9313, 9314 (word from Zhanaa); quest 9538 (Aurren, Totem of Akida at Azure Watch); DB spawns: Arugoo 17114, Totem of Akida 17360, Injured Night Elf Priestess 17117 in 3576; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Azure_Watch (Hand of Argus founded it, artificers built it); creature_text 16551 (Dyvuun at his emitter); quest 9313 reward text (both emitters fixed)'),
(352408, 1, 3524, 8, 0, 0, 'Moongraze Woods', 'North of Azure Watch, Moongraze Woods is home to herds of moongraze stags and bucks. Draenei hunters say the stags recall the talbuk their greatest hunters stalked on Draenor, though one draenei youngling out on the hunt grumbles that the two look nothing alike. The woods also hide a darker problem. Infected nightstalker runts prowl among the trees, and the sickened beasts behave strangely, though what ails them cannot be seen from the outside.', 'quest 9454 (moongraze stag resembles the talbuk); quest 10324 (bucks north of Azure Watch); creature_text 17587 (These stags look nothing like talbuks); quests 9455, 9456 (crystal in a nightstalker runt, crystal fragments in the river to the east, this is clearly our fault); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Exodar (nightstalkers ingested crystals, culled to stop corruption spreading across Moongraze Woods); DB spawns: Moongraze Buck, Stag, Infected Nightstalker Runt in 3916 (centre north-east of Azure Watch)'),
(352409, 1, 3524, 9, 0, 0, 'Emberglade', 'On the island''s northeast coast lies Emberglade, a sacred place of fire where scorched trees stand above smoldering ground and flaming aspects drift between them. Its guardian is Temper, a fire elemental of great power, who teaches that flame is renewal as well as destruction: it consumes what it burns, then dies, to be reborn another time. The crash of the Exodar unbalanced one of Temper''s own kind, Hauteur, who has gone mad and set himself up as a god among the owlbeasts, a thing no true elemental would do. Draenei shaman come here to be tested before shaping their first fire totems.', 'quest 9464 (sacred place of fire to the northeast on the coast, burned trees, Temper a fire elemental of great power); quest 9465 description and reward text (Hauteur gone insane because of the crash, flame consumes then dies to be reborn); quest 9467 reward text (reborn from his ashes); creature_text 17220 Hauteur Reborn; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Emberglade (burnt area, Flaming Aspects)'),
(352410, 1, 3524, 10, 0, 0, 'Stillpine Hold', 'Stillpine Hold is the cave home of the Stillpine furbolgs in the north of the isle, ruled by High Chief Stillpine. For centuries the tribe lived at peace with the creatures of the land, until the crystal storm fell from the sky. Then the wildkin, once their allies, went mad and stormed the hold with a beast of legend, the Kurken, at their side. Now the tribe holds only the ground before its own cave. Stillpine the Younger, heir to the tribe''s legacy, has set a death trap for the raving wildkin that pour out, and the bodies of defenders and wildkin lie where they fell. Why the wildkin turned is a question the high chief wants answered.', 'quest 9559 reward text (centuries of peace); quest 9565 (wildkin, once allies, attacked and took residence); quest 9570 (after the crystal storm, the Kurken brought by the invading wildkin); quest 9573 (Stillpine the Younger''s death trap, none of his defenders could get inside); quest 9566 (blood red crystal dissolving into the cave water); DB spawns: Stillpine Defender Corpse, Crazed Wildkin Corpse in 3572; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Stillpine_Hold'),
(352411, 1, 3524, 11, 0, 0, 'Menagerie Wreckage', 'Along the northeast beaches lie the shattered cages of the Exodar''s menagerie, scattered there when the ship came down. Ravagers were carried aboard as specimens, and with their cages broken the insect-like predators have spread into the forest. The Stillpine had never seen such creatures, and when ravagers ambushed two furbolg hunters, the leatherworker Moordo wondered aloud whether they heralded the end of the world. One of the deadliest, a death ravager, was still caged nearby, little armored but resistant to most magic, and draenei warriors were sent to free it from its prison and its pain with a plain blade. Blood elf bandits also lurk among the wreckage.', 'quest 9582 (menagerie scattered on the northeast beaches, death ravager resistant to magic, killed by a simple blade); quest 9560 (two Stillpine hunters ambushed by insect-like beasts never seen before, apocalypse); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Menagerie_Wreckage (cages destroyed, ravager specimens escaped into the forest); DB spawns: Ravager Specimen x37 and Blood Elf Bandit x4 in 3578'),
(352412, 1, 3524, 12, 0, 0, 'Silting Shore', 'The Silting Shore on the northwest coast belongs to the Siltfin murlocs. The Stillpine never trusted them, but in these dark days the murlocs have grown bold enough to raid Stillpine Hold and carry off its grain. One of them humiliated the furbolg Gurf in broad daylight, kicking him and spitting on him, and Gurf would dearly like news of a dark-skinned murloc with a patch of white fur stuck between its toes. A darker presence haunts these beaches too. A quel''dorei magewraith, a spirit consumed by its own magic, rises when spells are hurled carelessly along the shore, and draenei mages are sent to face it as a lesson in self-control.', 'quest 9562 description and request text (tenuous relationship, Siltfin stole food stores, Silting Shore to the west); quest 9564 (Gurf''s Dignity dropped by Murgurgula 17475); quest 9595 (northwest beaches, magewraith consumed by magic, lesson in control); creature_text 17612 Quel''dorei Magewraith; DB spawns: Siltfin murlocs, Murgurgula and a Quel''dorei Magewraith in 3575'),
(352413, 1, 3524, 13, 0, 0, 'Bristlelimb Village', 'Deep in the western woods, reached by an ancient elven road, stands Bristlelimb Village, home of the Bristlelimb furbolgs. The two furbolg tribes of the isle are at war, and the totems of the Stillpine record terrible deeds done to them by the Bristlelimb. Cages throughout the village hold Stillpine captives, and their captors, from hulking ursa to windcallers, hold the keys. The furbolg language totem that stands here bears the word vark, which means justice, and its carvings foretell a hero, not of furbolg blood, who will rise to save the Stillpine.', 'quest 9542 (furbolg den due west, ancient elven road); quest 9544 (war between Stillpine and Bristlelimb, keys from Bristlelimb furbolgs); quest 9542 reward text (Vark means justice); creature_text 17375 Stillpine Captive; DB spawns: Bristlelimb Furbolg, Ursa, Windcaller, Stillpine Captive, Bristlelimb Cage, Totem of Vark in 3571; quest 9544 description (prophecy carved on the Totem of Vark)'),
(352414, 1, 3524, 14, 0, 0, 'Odesyus'' Landing', 'Odesyus'' Landing is an Alliance camp on the southern shore of Azuremyst, set up by Admiral Odesyus of Alliance Naval Command after goblin stowaways forced his two ships into port. Loggers and axemen work the nearby forest while Stormwind marines stand guard. The camp gathers an unlikely company: ''Cookie'' McWeaksauce, a reformed pirate whose menu so often comes down to chicken that the admiral dreads asking about dinner; the dwarf Adamant Ironheart of the Explorers'' League; the night elf Priestess Kyleen Il''dinare; and a gnome engineer, Spark Overgrind, an envoy of High Tinker Mekkatorque who passes his days collecting shells along the beach.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Odesyus''_Landing (southern coast, two ships, NPC list); quest 9506 (forced to port, goblins in the holds of both ships); quest 9512 (reformed pirate, chicken); creature_text 17240 and 17246 (dinner banter); creature_text 17243 (seashells); creature_template subnames 17240, 17242, 17243; DB spawns: Alliance Axeman, Alliance Logger, Stormwind Marine in 3573'),
(352415, 1, 3524, 15, 0, 0, 'Geezle''s Camp', 'East of Odesyus'' Landing, Venture Company goblins have pitched a camp of their own in the thicket, under a boss named Geezle. They reached Azuremyst hidden in the holds of the admiral''s ships, struck one night while the crew slept below deck, and jumped ship with the fleet''s compass and charts. Saboteurs and gemologists now keep the camp, and the stolen gear lies somewhere among their tents.', 'quest 9506 description and reward text (stowaways, struck at night, navigation gear, thicket east of the landing, Mogul Razdunk''s orders); quest 9530 (plans document the conspiracy, a traitor among us); quest 9531 (Geezle leader of the goblins); DB spawns: Venture Co. Saboteur, Gemologist, Nautical Map and Compass in 3577; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Geezle''s_Camp'),
(352416, 1, 3524, 16, 0, 0, 'Wrathscale Point', 'West of Odesyus'' Landing lie the remains of an ancient night elf settlement, long abandoned and now overrun by the Wrathscale naga. Myrmidons and sirens prowl among the broken stones, and relics of the old kaldorei lie buried all through the ruins. On the coast nearby the naga also hold a cave, Tides'' Hollow. Some of the naga carry tablets covered in runes. To Priestess Kyleen Il''dinare these are the lands of her ancestors, and she will not see them tainted.', 'quest 9513 (ancient night elf city to the west, in ruin and overrun with naga, ancestral lands); quest 9523 and Ancient Relic objects in 3570; quest 9514 and creature_text 17242 (tablet: Sriss''tiz to take the island by force, reinforcements from Nazjatar); quest 9515 (hidden in a cave along the coast to the west); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Wrathscale_Point (small night elf ruin, Sriss''tiz executed at Tides'' Hollow); DB spawns: Wrathscale naga, myrmidons and sirens underground (z -28 to -41) beside Warlord Sriss''tiz, below the coast near the Tides'' Hollow cell 3569'),
(352417, 1, 3524, 17, 0, 0, 'Silvermyst Isle', 'Silvermyst Isle lies a short way off the southwest coast of Azuremyst. For years the night elf fisherman Cowlen lived here with his wife and daughter, at peace with the owlbeasts of the island. When crystal shards from the Exodar fell here, the owlbeasts of Moonwing Den went mad. With murlocs beside them they stormed the beach, razed Cowlen''s home and sank his ship, leaving him alone on the docks. Deranged and raving owlbeasts still fill Moonwing Den, and there the mad fire elemental Hauteur commanded them to burn an effigy in his honor and worship him as their god.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Silvermyst_Isle (southwest, swim, crystal shards drove the Moonwing wildkin mad); quests 9527, 9528 (lived peacefully among the owlbeasts, murlocs and owlkin attacked); npc_text of Cowlen (home razed, ship sunk); quest 10428 (southeast docks of Silvermyst Isle); quest 9467 (Moonwing Den owlbeasts worship Hauteur, burn an effigy); DB: Wickerman Effigy 181672 in 3566; Deranged, Raving and Aberrant Owlbeasts in 3639/3566'),
(352418, 1, 3524, 18, 0, 0, 'Valaar''s Berth', 'Valaar''s Berth is the dock on Azuremyst''s western shore, south of the Exodar, where the ship Elune''s Blessing comes in from Auberdine on the Darkshore coast. For the draenei it is the door to the rest of Kalimdor and to the allies they hoped to find there. For travelers sailing the other way, it is a first glimpse of the strangers who fell from the sky. Beyond the pier, skittering crawlers pick their way along the sand.', 'transports table guid 9: Auberdine, Darkshore and Valaar''s Berth, Azuremyst Isle (Boat, Alliance, Elune''s Blessing); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Azuremyst_Isle (Valaar''s Berth is the boat dock); DB spawn: Skittering Crawler in 3574 at about -4253, -11405 (west coast, south of the Exodar); quest 9505 (allies would find us on this island)'),
(352419, 2, 3524, 1, 1, 0, 'Exarch Menelaous', 'Exarch Menelaous commands Azure Watch, the draenei outpost within sight of the wreck of the Exodar. Gazing at the broken ship, he says it is hard to imagine that anyone survived such a catastrophe. He speaks of ten lifetimes spent fleeing the madness of the Burning Legion, and swears that here at last the draenei will stop running and make their stand, though he is ready to die for it, for the Prophet holds that it is here their fate will finally be known. Reports of trouble from every corner of the isle cross his desk, and those that matter go on to Velen.', 'npc_text of Exarch Menelaous 17116 (ten lifetimes fleeing the Legion, no more running, I am ready to die); quests 9455, 9456; quest 9616 reward text (bounty on draenei, Velen will be informed); quest 9602 reward text (spy, will notify Velen); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Exarch_Menelaous'),
(352420, 2, 3524, 2, 1, 0, 'Vindicator Aldar', 'Vindicator Aldar watches over the survivors at the Crash Site in Ammen Vale. He tells young draenei that the Light offers many paths, and that each of them must choose which to walk on this world or any other. He set the vale''s first recovery in motion, sending helpers to inoculate the owlkin around the salvage and scouts up to Shadow Ridge, where reports of unusual activity trouble him, for one of his scouts has not reported back.', 'npc_text of Vindicator Aldar 16535 (many are the paths of the Light); quest 9303 (inoculation); quest 9309 (one of my scouts); quest 9798 reward text (blood elves followed us, evil to the core, apology); quest 9311 completion text'),
(352421, 2, 3524, 3, 1, 0, 'Admiral Odesyus', 'Admiral Odesyus of Alliance Naval Command was at sea with two ships when goblin stowaways struck one night, stole his navigation gear and jumped ship, forcing him into port on Azuremyst. Embarrassed even to speak of it, he has made camp on the southern shore, and help in getting his compass and charts back would, he says, make for a strong gesture. Between crises he trades weary banter with his cook, whose grand promises for dinner always end in chicken, and he assures his helpers that he is taking care of everything.', 'quest 9506 description and reward text (both ships, navigation gear, off course, I smell a traitor); quests 9530, 9531 (none of my crew can be trusted, tree disguise); creature_text 17240 and 17246 (dinner banter, it be chicken); creature_template 17240 subname Alliance Naval Command'),
(352422, 2, 3524, 4, 0, 0, 'Engineer Spark Overgrind', 'Engineer Spark Overgrind came to Azuremyst as an envoy of High Tinker Mekkatorque, sailing with Admiral Odesyus, and he now waits at Odesyus'' Landing while the admiral''s ships sit in port. He passes his days hunting seashells along the beach, examining each find, holding the biggest to his ear and tucking them into his pack, and he confesses that he hates the ocean but loves the beach. Those who interrupt him are told he is busy.', 'creature_text 17243 (seashells, meeting with Geezle, Velen left open, the Legion''s servants, die by the will of Kael''thas); creature_template 17243 subname Envoy of Mekkatorque; quest 9531 reward text (it was the gnome); quest 9537; page_text 2919-2920 (Kael''thas: MY vessel, only link able to repair the Exodar); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Engineer_%22Spark%22_Overgrind; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Engineer_%22Spark%22_Overgrind (travelling with Odesyus, emissary of Mekkatorque)'),
(352423, 2, 3524, 5, 1, 0, 'Priestess Kyleen Il''dinare', 'Priestess Kyleen Il''dinare is a night elf servant of Elune staying at Odesyus'' Landing, and she makes no secret of her suspicion of the draenei. Her people, she says, know much of the newcomers'' forebears, and in appearance they resemble the eredar far too closely. Still, she senses that fate has pushed them all toward this island for a reason. The ruins to the west were once the lands of her ancestors, and she cannot bear to see them fouled by the Wrathscale naga, whose kind she has seen at their worst.', 'npc_text of Priestess Kyleen Il''dinare 17241 (eyes you suspiciously, similarities to the eredar, tenuous path); quest 9513 (invisible hand of fate, ancestral lands, Elune be praised); quest 9515 description and reward text (I''ve seen what naga can do, I was wrong to think badly of you, Archimonde, gift from the night elves); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Priestess_Kyleen_Il''dinare'),
(352424, 2, 3524, 6, 1, 0, 'Archaeologist Adamant Ironheart', 'Adamant Ironheart of the Explorers'' League is a dwarf of Ironforge who once served in its elite guard, and he will tell anyone who listens that he was Magni''s right-hand man. Retired now, he took up archaeology as a hobby and a fine excuse to see the world. His pappy always said that where there are night elf ruins, night elf relics are sure to be close by, so the ruins at Wrathscale Point thrill him, and he promises his diggers that Ironforge will hear all about them.', 'npc_text of Adamant Ironheart 17242 (Ironforge elite guard, Magni''s right hand man, retired, archaeology hobby); quest 9523 description and reward text (pappy, relics, they''ll learn about you in Ironforge); creature_text 17242 (Anything for you, darling; reads the tablet); creature_template 17242 subname Explorers'' League'),
(352425, 2, 3524, 7, 1, 0, 'High Chief Stillpine', 'High Chief Stillpine rules the Stillpine furbolgs of Azuremyst. His tribe lived in peace with the creatures of the land for centuries, until the omens of Kurz the Revelator warned that the gods would shatter the land and turn friend and foe alike against the Stillpine, and that a hero not of Stillpine blood, the Promised One, would deliver them. Then the crystal storm came, and the maddened wildkin drove his people out of their own hold. His first concern is the root of that corruption, and he sends the Promised One into the cave to find it.', 'quest 9559 reward text (centuries of peace, Kurz''s dark omens, gods would shatter the land, the Promised One); quest 9565 (root of the corruption); quest 9622 (hold saved, people return to their ancestral home, darkness looms for your people, aid of the Stillpine); npc_text of High Chief Stillpine 17440'),
(352426, 2, 3524, 8, 1, 0, 'Kurz the Revelator', 'Kurz the Revelator is the seer of the Stillpine. Several months ago he began to see dark omens of a catastrophe that would end the tribe''s long peace, and of a hero not of Stillpine blood who would rise to deliver them. When the crystal storm had passed, a beast of myth called the Kurken came into the village with the invading wildkin and slew many furbolgs who tried to stand against it. Kurz has seen in his visions the one who will bring it down, and he greets the draenei champion as the Promised One.', 'quest 9559 reward text (several months ago Kurz began to see dark omens, hero not of Stillpine blood); quest 9570 description and reward text (crystal storm, the Kurken, I have seen one defeat the Kurken); npc_text of Kurz 17443 (the Promised One has arrived); quest 9622 reward text (they saw the power core of the Exodar and O''ros)'),
(352427, 2, 3524, 9, 0, 0, 'Warlord Sriss''tiz', 'Warlord Sriss''tiz leads the Wrathscale naga who have overrun the night elf ruins of Wrathscale Point on Azuremyst''s southern coast. While his myrmidons and sirens prowl the broken stones above, he keeps to Tides'' Hollow, a cave along the coast to the west of Odesyus'' Landing, and lashes out with watery strikes at any who come close. To Priestess Kyleen Il''dinare, the ruins his naga hold are the lands of her ancestors.', 'creature_text 17242 (tablet: Sriss''tiz ordered his naga to take the rest of the island by force, reinforcements from Nazjatar); quest 9515 description and reward text; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Wrathscale_Point (Sriss''tiz executed at Tides'' Hollow)'),
(352428, 3, 3524, 1, 1, 0, 'Survivors of the Crash', 'Weeks after the Exodar fell, the last draenei lying in suspension in Ammen Vale began to wake to a ruined world. Proenitus, unsure why the ship crashed, knows only that there is little time to save whoever can still be saved. The healing crystals are spent, and the only substitute at hand is the blood of the vale moths, an unhappy necessity for a people who shun needless killing. The vials go to the priest Zalduun, who sends the able out to find the injured by the red glow of crystal radiation and heal them with the gift of the naaru. Botanist Taerix wants the volatile creatures near the fallen cores culled and the mutated lashers studied, hoping to heal the poisoned lake. Travelers of the Alliance who reach the vale are pressed into the same work.', 'quests 9279, 9280, 9369, 9409, 9283 descriptions and reward texts; creature_text 16483 Draenei Survivor; quests 10302, 9293, 9294; quest 9369 AllowableRaces 77 (human, dwarf, night elf, gnome)'),
(352429, 3, 3524, 2, 1, 0, 'The Blood Elves of Shadow Ridge', 'Even as survivors gather at the Crash Site, reports of strange activity on Shadow Ridge keep reaching Vindicator Aldar, though his people believed their scouting of the vale thorough. One of his scouts, Tolaan, has not come back, and Aldar sends help southwest across Silverline Lake to find him and learn what has delayed him. The survivors are few and battered, and they need time: time to tend their wounded and to repair the emitter that may yet reach other draenei beyond the vale.', 'quests 9309, 10303, 9311 descriptions, reward and completion texts; creature_text 16522 Surveyor Candress; page_text 2906 (Blood Elf Plans); quests 9798, 9312, 9313; creature_text 17268 and 16551 (Zhanaa and Dyvuun on the emitter)'),
(352430, 3, 3524, 3, 1, 0, 'The Sleeping Priestess', 'A night elf priestess was found injured and unconscious beside the Crystalbrook only the day before, and carried to Azure Watch, a delicate guest among so many injured draenei passing through that healing ointments are always in short supply. Anchorite Fateema has found that the vines of the island''s lashers hold restorative properties, and believes that with proper treatment they can be broken down into an ointment strong enough to save her. There is little time to lose, for Fateema fears that the priestess''s health is in steady decline.', 'quests 9463, 9473, 9505 descriptions and reward texts; creature_text 17117 Injured Night Elf Priestess; creature_text 17214 (Man''ari, we are not eredar); creature_text 17215 Daedal; quest 9505 reward text (Odesyus: one of our crew)'),
(352431, 3, 3524, 4, 1, 0, 'The Traitor of Odesyus'' Landing', 'Admiral Odesyus of Alliance Naval Command has a problem he finds embarrassing even to talk about. Venture Company goblins stowed away in the holds of both his ships, struck one night while most of the crew slept below deck, and jumped ship with his compass and charts, forcing him into port on Azuremyst. They vanished into the thicket east of his camp, and the admiral asks any willing stranger to go after the stolen gear, for it would make a strong gesture.', 'quests 9506, 9530, 9531, 9537, 9602 descriptions and reward texts; creature_text 17243 and 17318 (the meeting); page_text 2919-2920 (Traitor''s Communication); DB: naga flag object 181694 at Traitor''s Cove (posarea 3579)'),
(352432, 3, 3524, 5, 1, 0, 'The Promised One', 'At Azure Watch, Cryptographer Aurren has found that the language of the Stillpine furbolgs is carved into their totems, and Arugoo of the Stillpine waits beside the first of them. Following the totems one by one, up a hill, across the Crystalbrook and down to the riverbed, a reader learns the tongue until it reads like their own, and the last of them stands in Bristlelimb Village, where the Bristlelimb keep Stillpine furbolgs in cages. The carvings tell of a war between the two tribes, of terrible deeds done to the Stillpine, and of a prophecy: a hero not of furbolg blood will rise to save them.', 'quests 9538, 9539, 9540, 9541, 9542, 9544, 9559, 9565, 9566, 9570, 9573, 9622 descriptions and reward texts'),
(352433, 3, 3524, 6, 1, 0, 'All That Remains', 'On Silvermyst Isle, off the southwest coast of Azuremyst, the night elf fisherman Cowlen lived for years with his wife and daughter by the docks on the island''s southeastern shore, at peace with the owlbeasts around them. Several weeks ago that peace ended. Owlbeasts maddened by the crystals that fell from the Exodar stormed the beach with murlocs beside them and fell upon the family, and the home they had made there was destroyed. Deranged owlbeasts still fill Moonwing Den in the island''s heart.', 'quests 10428, 9527, 9528 descriptions, reward and completion texts; npc_text of Cowlen 17311 (broken man, take my life); creature_text 17312 Magwin and 17311 Cowlen; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Cowlen'),
(352434, 3, 3524, 7, 1, 0, 'The Draenei Call of Fire', 'When a young draenei shaman is ready to learn the ways of flame, Tuluun of Azure Watch sends them to Emberglade to face Temper, a fire elemental of great power. Temper has a trouble of his own. The crash of the Exodar drove one of his brethren, Hauteur, insane, and the fallen elemental now demands that the owlbeasts of Silvermyst Isle worship him, something no true elemental would ever do. The balance must be restored, and the shaman''s first task is to win back the ritual torch that the crazed wildkin have carried into Stillpine Hold.', 'quests 9462, 9464, 9465, 9467, 9468 descriptions and reward texts; quest 9461 (Velen asks for the shaman); creature_text 17220 Hauteur Reborn');
INSERT INTO `mod_lore_codex_part` (`Entry`, `Part`, `MinState`, `MaxState`, `Body`, `Sources`) VALUES
(352400, 1, 0, 255, 'The trouble on the isle ran deeper than it seemed. A letter taken from a traitor showed who stood behind the plotting: Kael''thas Sunstrider, signing himself king, who called the Exodar his own vessel, wanted it repaired, and ordered a full assault on the draenei to take it back. An eredar agent, her identity still unknown to the draenei, had already sent him word of where the ship lay.', 'page_text 2919-2920 (Traitor''s Communication: MY vessel, eredar agent transmitted the Exodar''s location, identity still a mystery, full scale assault, repair the Exodar, signed King Sunstrider); quest 9602 description (plans of Kael''thas), shown on turning in 9537'),
(352402, 1, 0, 255, 'In time the emitter did its work. Word from Zhanaa reached Azure Watch across the Crystalbrook, and the two camps found each other: survivors still lived in Ammen Vale, and their kin were waiting beyond the river.', 'quest 9312 reward text and smart_scripts 1707100 (the emitter works, an image of Technician Dyvuun appears); quest 9314 description and reward text (Azure Watch received word from Zhanaa, the survivors we''ve been hearing about)'),
(352403, 1, 0, 255, 'Taerix''s theory held. From the samples she devised a neutralizing agent, and once it was scattered beside the crystal the poison seemed to lift. No one knows how long it will last, and Taerix wishes the crystal could be pulled from the lake entirely.', 'quest 9294 description and reward text'),
(352405, 1, 0, 255, 'Tolaan was found on the ridge, gravely wounded and barely able to speak. Blood elves had ambushed him, and with what breath he has left he urges that the threat on the ridge be dealt with before it reaches the survivors.', 'quest 9309 reward text; quest 10303 description and completion text'),
(352405, 2, 0, 255, 'The orders Surveyor Candress carried told what the party was for: survey the extent of the islands and report back, and on no account be caught. They were signed with a single letter, S. The blood elves had followed the draenei all the way to Azeroth.', 'page_text 2906 (Blood Elf Plans, signed S.); item 24414 drops from 16522 and starts quest 9798'),
(352408, 1, 0, 255, 'The cause lay in their bellies. A runt was found with a faintly glowing crystal inside it, a piece of the Exodar, and Exarch Menelaous admitted the fault was his people''s: reports of crushed crystal in the river to the east had been ignored too long. He has ordered the infected nightstalkers culled before the contamination spreads any further.', 'quest 9455 description and reward text; quest 9456 description'),
(352409, 1, 0, 255, 'Temper''s teaching proved true of Hauteur himself. Slain beside the effigy his worshippers burned for him, the mad elemental was reborn from his own ashes, and he now burns beside Temper at Emberglade, brighter than ever before and, it seems, a little reluctant to speak.', 'quest 9467 reward text; creature_text 17220 Hauteur Reborn'),
(352410, 1, 0, 255, 'Deep inside the hold lay the answer: a crystal from the Exodar, blood red and rapidly dissolving into the water supply of the cave, radiating a sickly aura. Something has gone terribly wrong with it, and it may explain why the creatures of Azuremyst have turned so savage.', 'quest 9565 reward text; quest 9566 description; gameobject 181748 ends 9565 and starts 9566'),
(352410, 2, 0, 255, 'With the Kurken slain, High Chief Stillpine declares the hold saved. His people will soon make their way back to their ancestral home, and he hails a new age of prosperity for the Stillpine.', 'quest 9622 description (the Hold is saved, return to the ancestral home); quest 9622 PrevQuestID 9570 (the Kurken)'),
(352412, 1, 0, 255, 'The culprit was Murgurgula, the fearsome brute of the Siltfin. When he fell, the white fur between his toes was found to be a clump of Gurf''s own, ''lost'' in his struggle with the murlocs, and so what remained of Gurf''s dignity could at last be carried home to him.', 'quest 9564 description; item 23850 Gurf''s Dignity drops from Murgurgula 17475'),
(352415, 1, 0, 255, 'Rolled inside the stolen map were orders from Mogul Razdunk, and they were blunt: strip-mine the island of the Exodar''s crystal wreckage, then hijack the Alliance ships once the work was done. The goblins knew far too much of the admiral''s plans, and the papers left him sure that someone in his own crew was in league with them.', 'quest 9506 reward text; quest 9530 description'),
(352416, 1, 0, 255, 'One of those tablets was a naga communication, and Adamant Ironheart read it out: their warlord, Sriss''tiz, has ordered his naga to take the rest of the island by force, and reinforcements are coming from Nazjatar. Kyleen, who had brought him the tablet, thanked him and said she knew just the person for the job.', 'creature_text 17241 and 17242, smart_scripts 1724100 (the tablet scene on turning in 9514); item 23759 drops from naga 17193-17195'),
(352419, 1, 0, 255, 'When a crystal from the Exodar turned up inside a sickened nightstalker, Menelaous made no excuses. Reports of crushed crystal fragments in the river to the east had been ignored, he admitted, and the fault was his people''s. Rather than sit and mourn the harm done to the land, he ordered the infected beasts culled before it could spread.', 'quest 9455 reward text; quest 9456 description'),
(352419, 2, 0, 255, 'A ledger taken from blood elf bandits showed a price on draenei heads, drawn as a slain draenei with a smiling elf standing over the corpse. By the beardless, geometric head of O''ros, the exarch swore: these blood elves are out for blood, and Velen will be told at once.', 'quest 9616 description and reward text; item 23910 drops from Blood Elf Bandit 17591'),
(352419, 3, 0, 255, 'Worse news came from Odesyus'' Landing: a letter taken from a gnome traitor in the service of Kael''thas. Reading it, Menelaous cursed them all to the Nether, for it showed that a spy had been watching everything the draenei did, for who knows how long. He took the warning straight to Velen.', 'quest 9602 reward text'),
(352420, 1, 0, 255, 'Then it was true: a scouting party of blood elves in Ammen Vale itself. With their surveyor slain, Aldar promised to deal with whatever remnant of them was still nearby and sent for Tolaan to be brought back, but he could not understand how the sin''dorei had followed his people so far.', 'quest 9311 completion and reward text'),
(352420, 2, 0, 255, 'The plans taken from the surveyor broke his composure. The blood elves have followed us here, he cried; they are evil to the core and should be wiped from existence. Then he caught himself and apologized, a rare crack in a vindicator''s discipline.', 'quest 9798 reward text'),
(352421, 1, 0, 255, 'The theft was no prank. Orders found rolled in the map showed the goblins meant to strip-mine the island''s crystal wreckage and then seize his fleet, and the admiral smelled a traitor: only someone close to him could have told them his plans. Trusting none of his crew, he turned to newcomers on the isle and devised an absurd scheme involving a hollowed-out tree and a pile of leaves.', 'quest 9506 reward text; quest 9530 description'),
(352421, 2, 0, 255, 'The scheme worked. Disguised as a tree, an observer watched the goblin boss meet his contact, and the admiral could hardly believe the answer: it was the gnome all along, the envoy of Mekkatorque. If so high an official of the Alliance could turn traitor, he wondered, how many others might be corrupt?', 'quest 9531 reward text; quest 9537 description'),
(352422, 1, 0, 255, 'His beachcombing was a cover. Spark was the traitor in league with the Venture Company. At a secret meeting at a cove in the west, marked by a naga flag, he berated their boss Geezle for leaving the stolen compass and charts in plain view, spoke of a spy on the inside, warned what Kael''thas does to those who fail him, and boasted that Velen would soon leave himself open to attack.', 'creature_text 17243 and 17318 (the meeting); quest 9531 description and reward text'),
(352422, 2, 0, 255, 'Unmasked on the beach, Spark laughed, and taunted that devoted servants of the Legion live quietly within every civilization until they are called upon. Live in fear, die by the will of Kael''thas, he said, and drew his blade. He fell fighting, and a letter on his body showed that Kael''thas meant him to repair the Exodar and return it to its self-proclaimed owner.', 'creature_text 17243 (confrontation, smart_scripts 1724300); page_text 2919-2920'),
(352423, 1, 0, 255, 'Once Warlord Sriss''tiz was dead, Kyleen''s doubts gave way. The threat of a naga invasion is only a distant memory now, she says, and the isle is safe, for the time being. She admits she was wrong to think badly of the draenei, who show nothing of the filth that was Archimonde, and offers them a gift from the night elves.', 'quest 9515 reward text'),
(352424, 1, 0, 255, 'When Priestess Kyleen brought him a rune covered tablet, he answered with gallantry, ''anything for you, darling'', and read it slowly in the naga''s own tongue. Naga warlord, he groaned, and told her she would not like it: Warlord Sriss''tiz had ordered his naga to take the rest of the island by force, with reinforcements coming from Nazjatar.', 'creature_text 17241 and 17242 (the tablet scene)'),
(352425, 1, 0, 255, 'With the hold saved, his people can make their way back to their ancestral home, and he hails a new age of prosperity for the Stillpine. Yet he warns that darkness looms ahead for the draenei, with questions left unanswered, and he promises the Promised One the tribe''s aid whenever it is asked for.', 'quest 9622 description'),
(352426, 1, 0, 255, 'His vision held true. The Kurken fell in the depths of Stillpine Hold, and when its hide was brought to him, Kurz proclaimed that the Promised One had emerged victorious and that the prophecy was nearly complete, then turned at once to the matter of the beast''s hide.', 'quest 9570 reward text'),
(352426, 2, 0, 255, 'The prophecy has come to pass, but the visions of the Stillpine have shown something stranger still, and word of it was carried back to the draenei: the power core of the Exodar, and the naaru O''ros. What it means, not even Exarch Menelaous can say.', 'quest 9622 description and reward text'),
(352427, 1, 0, 255, 'Orders carried by his warriors laid out his ambition: to take the rest of the island by force, with more naga coming from Nazjatar to swell his ranks. Priestess Kyleen, who has seen what naga can do, fears an invasion would be a catastrophe for every being on the isle, and wants the warlord''s reign ended before his reinforcements arrive.', 'creature_text 17242 (tablet); quest 9515 description'),
(352427, 2, 0, 255, 'Sriss''tiz fell at last in the depths of Tides'' Hollow, struck down in the cave where he had kept himself hidden. Whatever he planned for Azuremyst, the Wrathscale who hold the ruins above have lost their warlord.', 'quest 9515 objective (kill Warlord Sriss''tiz)'),
(352428, 1, 0, 255, 'One by one the survivors were found and healed. They stagger up asking where they are and what became of the ship, or remembering only the fall and the scramble for the pods, then go to help the others. Zalduun praised the work as only a true hero could have done it.', 'creature_text 16483 Draenei Survivor; quest 9283 reward text'),
(352428, 2, 0, 255, 'Taerix''s study gave her an answer: a neutralizing agent, scattered beside the crystal in Silverline Lake. It worked, though she cannot say for how long, and she wishes the crystal could be removed entirely. Meanwhile she would have Tedon try the agent on one of the captured beasts at once.', 'quest 9294 reward text'),
(352429, 1, 0, 255, 'Tolaan was found on the ridge, gravely wounded and barely able to speak: blood elves had ambushed him. A whole party of their scouts holds the ridge, determined that no draenei will leave the vale alive, and with what strength he has left Tolaan urges that their numbers be thinned.', 'quest 9309 reward text; quest 10303 description; creature_text 16521 Blood Elf Scout'),
(352429, 2, 0, 255, 'Thinning them was not enough, so Tolaan urged that their leader, Surveyor Candress, be slain, in the hope that the rest would pull back and buy time for the repairs. Candress died refusing to be taken alive. Aldar could not understand how the sin''dorei had followed his people so far, and promised to deal with whatever was left of them.', 'quest 10303 reward text; quest 9311 description, completion and reward text; creature_text 16522 Surveyor Candress'),
(352429, 3, 0, 255, 'The orders Candress carried, signed with a single letter, S., showed why the party had come: to survey the extent of the islands and report back, and on no account to be caught.', 'page_text 2906 (Blood Elf Plans)'),
(352429, 4, 0, 255, 'Soon after, the repairs were done. Technician Zhanaa''s emitter flickered to life, and a faint, crackling voice answered her from beyond the Crystalbrook: Technician Dyvuun, at Azure Watch. Their kin beyond the vale were alive.', 'quest 9312 reward text; creature_text 17268 and 16551'),
(352430, 1, 0, 255, 'The ointment was not enough. Fateema applied it to the priestess''s wounds and found it ineffective, and the alchemist Daedal turned instead to the azure snapdragon, a rare bloom some call a cure for every ill, which grows at the foot of the island''s azure pines and is eaten by the root threshers.', 'creature_text 17214, smart_scripts 1721400 (ointment ineffective, on turning in 9463); quest 9473 description'),
(352430, 2, 0, 255, 'The remedy roused her, briefly. The priestess sat up, saw who stood around her and cried out against cursed eredar, warning that she had not come alone, before slipping back into her coma. To be taken for the man''ari stung the draenei deeply. Daedal remembered words of the Prophet: on this island their allies would find them, but they would be tested and asked to pay for the sins of their fathers. He sent a messenger south to find her people.', 'creature_text 17117, 17214, 17215, smart_scripts 1721500 (the waking, on turning in 9473); quest 9505 description'),
(352430, 3, 0, 255, 'The messenger found them at Odesyus'' Landing on the southern shore, where Admiral Odesyus recognized the sleeping priestess as one of his own crew and sent a crewman to Azure Watch at once to see to her.', 'quest 9505 reward text'),
(352431, 1, 0, 255, 'Rolled inside the recovered map were orders from Mogul Razdunk: strip-mine the island''s crystal wreckage, then hijack the Alliance ships. The goblins knew too much, and the admiral concluded that someone close to him had sold him out. Trusting no one in his crew, he called for a hollowed-out tree and a pile of leaves.', 'quest 9506 reward text; quest 9530 description'),
(352431, 2, 0, 255, 'The tree was a disguise. Wearing it at a cove in the west where a naga flag marked a secret meeting, a spy hidden in plain sight watched Geezle meet his contact: Spark Overgrind, envoy of Mekkatorque and servant of Kael''thas, who boasted that Velen would soon leave himself open to attack.', 'quest 9531 description; creature_text 17243 and 17318 (the meeting); DB: naga flag object 181694 at Traitor''s Cove (posarea 3579)'),
(352431, 3, 0, 255, 'Confronted on the beach, the gnome fought to the death. The letter he carried, from Kael''thas himself, told of an eredar agent, still unknown to the draenei, who had revealed the Exodar''s location, and called for a full assault to take back the ship. The admiral judged that the news must reach the king and the draenei leaders.', 'page_text 2919-2920 (Traitor''s Communication); quest 9537 reward text'),
(352431, 4, 0, 255, 'The letter went on to Exarch Menelaous at Azure Watch, who cursed them all to the Nether: a spy had been watching everything the draenei did. He took the warning to Velen, and bade the messenger stand ready for the Prophet''s instructions.', 'quest 9602 reward text'),
(352432, 1, 0, 255, 'Those freed from the Bristlelimb cages hailed their rescuer, crying that the prophecy was true, and back at Azure Watch Arugoo humbled himself before the hero whose coming the spirits themselves had heralded. The prophecy of Akida, he said, had delivered a hero to the Stillpine.', 'creature_text 17375 Stillpine Captive; quest 9544 completion and reward text'),
(352432, 2, 0, 255, 'Named the Promised One and sent north to Stillpine Hold, the hero found it overrun by maddened wildkin, and deep inside lay the root of the trouble: a crystal of the Exodar, blood red and dissolving into the cave''s water, its sickly aura perhaps the cause of the savagery spreading across Azuremyst.', 'quest 9559 description and reward text (Promised One, go north); quest 9565 reward text; quest 9566 description'),
(352432, 3, 0, 255, 'Within the hold the Kurken, the beast of myth that came with the wildkin and slew so many Stillpine, was slain as Kurz the Revelator had foreseen, and the seer declared the prophecy nearly complete.', 'quest 9570 description and reward text'),
(352432, 4, 0, 255, 'Deeper in the hold, Chieftain Oomooroo of the crazed wildkin fell. Stillpine the Younger, whose defenders had never managed to fight their way inside, saw the opening he had waited for and sent an attack into the hold at once.', 'quest 9573 description and reward text'),
(352432, 5, 0, 255, 'With the hold saved, the Stillpine could return to their ancestral home. The high chief pledged his tribe''s aid to the Promised One and warned that darkness waited for the draenei too. When the tale reached Exarch Menelaous, it was the visions that puzzled him most: the Stillpine had seen the power core of the Exodar, and the naaru O''ros.', 'quest 9622 description and reward text'),
(352433, 1, 0, 255, 'Word of it reached Azure Watch in an unlikely way. In her fevered dreams the injured night elf priestess spoke of a fisherman, Cowlen, in some distress on Silvermyst Isle, and with so much else happening no one had looked into it. Dulvi, uneasy, asked a willing stranger to go.', 'quest 10428 description'),
(352433, 2, 0, 255, 'Cowlen was found on the docks, a broken man. He had fought until he was beaten senseless, and woke to sand soaked red with blood, his home razed and his ship sunk; his wife and daughter, he believed, had been devoured. He begged the stranger to end his life. He wanted no vengeance, only his family''s remains for a proper burial.', 'quest 10428 reward text; quest 9527 description; npc_text 8870 Cowlen'),
(352433, 3, 0, 255, 'Yet his daughter, Magwin, had escaped. Lost for weeks and sure that both her parents were dead, she was led home through the thicket, and father and daughter were reunited on the shore. Weeping for joy, Cowlen gave her rescuer a night elf heirloom, a token of friendship, trust and love, and named that stranger family until the end of time.', 'quest 9528 description and reward text; creature_text 17312 Magwin and 17311 Cowlen'),
(352434, 1, 0, 255, 'The torch is the mark of Hauteur''s arrogance: a flame that never goes out. Flame is meant to consume what it burns and then die, Temper teaches, to be reborn another time. The torch must burn a while longer all the same, for with it the shaman can light the effigy the owlbeasts of Moonwing Den burn in Hauteur''s honor, and when he answers, put the fallen elemental out of his misery.', 'quest 9465 reward text; quest 9467 description'),
(352434, 2, 0, 255, 'Hauteur came to his effigy and was destroyed, and his ashes were carried back to Emberglade. Death is no ending for fire: in destroying Hauteur the shaman also saved him, and reborn from his ashes he now burns beside Temper, brighter than before.', 'quest 9467 reward text; creature_text 17220 Hauteur Reborn'),
(352434, 3, 0, 255, 'Part of the ashes was set aside for the shaman''s fire totem. Tuluun saw in the trial a cleansing fire of destruction and renewal, not unlike the tribulation the draenei themselves are undergoing. Yet before the totem could be made, word came that the Prophet himself had heard of the shaman''s success and asked to see them.', 'quest 9468 description and reward text; quest 9461 description (shown on turning in 9468)');
